# Integer16 addition promotes overflow to int32

Adds 1 to the int16 maximum to verify the result promotes to int32 instead
of failing, then adds 1 again to verify chained arithmetic keeps using the
promoted representation. Both declarations keep the static int16 type while
the runtime values use the wider precision.

>>> source
maximum: int16 = 32767
unit: int16 = 1

overflow: int16 = maximum + unit
print(overflow)

chained: int16 = overflow + unit
print(chained)

<<< stdout
32768
32769

<<< stderr
